# Model weights — the detector (.pt + .onnx) is small (~16 MB total) and
# committed for zero-friction deploys. The ONNX copy is what the server loads
# on Render (onnxruntime — light); the .pt is the torch fallback. Keep
# last.pt (final-epoch checkpoint) and future classifiers out for now.
*.pt
*.onnx
!snail_detector.pt
!snail_detector.onnx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Booth pin mode — reference PHOTOS stay local (the pinned results are for
# the science-fair booth, not the repo). demo_pins.json IS committed: since
# build_demo_pins.py bakes the reference hashes into it, the deployed booth
# API (snail-api-booth) can load pins without the photos.
demo_pins/
